docs/cross-project/git-gatekeeper-design.md:8:**Implementation status:** branch protection and the account layout are LIVE (applied 2026-07-21; layout amendment ruled 2026-08-09, § The credential and enforcement, not yet applied). `scripts/git-gatekeeper.py` is BUILT through slice 4 of five (2026-08-08/09, per the build order in `docs/issues/3-git-gatekeeper-build-slice-plan.md`; a sixth slice — the review-evidence check — was added by ruling 2026-08-10 as a prerequisite of activating the privileged lane and is NOT yet built, its evidence format undesigned, § Open): the synchronous check-in, the entry checkpoint, and concurrent-check-in integration are running behavior (slice 2's `imports` table subcommand was built, then deleted by ruling 2026-08-10 — the trailer plus `git log --grep` is the view), exercised by a 169-case suite against throwaway repositories (the count moves as slices land; slices 4 and 5 added the lifecycle and audit cases). Slice 4 (the worker lifecycle: `--no-wait` with a detached worker, `status`, `cancel`, the opportunistic expiry sweep) is BUILT 2026-08-12. Slice 5 is BUILT 2026-08-12, completing the five-slice build: the `audit` subcommand answers B3c's three outcomes (protection-ok / protection-wrong with facts naming every differing setting / audit-failed) and rides each session recycle via the fast-handoff writer; the repo git-config pins (user.name, user.email, user.useConfigOnly) are set and test-pinned. The CLAUDE.md workflow line landed the same day, user-walked: the permanent path stated, the dormancy named, the interim lane described — activation day deletes its middle sentence. On this box the live audit answers `audit-failed` honestly: the agent credential cannot read protection settings — the audit reads green only under a credential that can, which arrives with the C-work. The gate is **dormant**: no host yet holds a main-capable credential for it (§ The credential and enforcement).
docs/cross-project/git-gatekeeper-design.md:16:One program, `scripts/git-gatekeeper.py`, is the only way any change reaches main. It holds the project's one **main-capable** credential (this section states the contract; the credential is dormant until it exists — see Implementation status). Agents — all of them, equally — invoke the program directly and never push to main themselves (branch pushes stay open to agent tokens — C4). One program, one credential, one door. No agent has a doorman or relay role in another agent's check-in path; choirmaster is simply the most frequent requester.
